BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Beginner Knitting Course - November
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20261115T123000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20261115T140000
UID:bistitchual-10402453258498@bistitchual.ca
DESCRIPTION:This listing is for a three session Beginner Knitting Course. 
 The classes will be held in person at Bistitchual on Sunday November 15th\
 , 22nd and 29th from 12:30-2:00pm Have you always wanted to learn to knit?
  We’ve got you covered! Beginner Knitting is a course for brand new begi
 nners\, and over these three 1.5hr classes\, Mike will teach you everythin
 g you need to create a basic project from beginning to end. Our class size
  is capped at 4 people\, so everyone can receive the attention they need. 
 Mike will share lots of tips and techniques to get you well on your way. (
 No experience necessary) Materials: Yarn and needles will be provided. Wha
 t We’ll Learn - How to make a slip knot. - Casting on. - The Knit stitch
 . - The Purl stitch. - Exploring Knit / Purl combinations. - Binding off. 
 - Weaving in ends. - Fixing common mistakes and how to avoid them. - Commo
 n uses of flat knitting. - Intro into Ravelry. Please note that classes wi
 ll only proceed if we have a minimum of two attendees . If the minimum is 
 not met\, there will be the option for a refund or to reschedule. There wi
 ll be a four person maximum for each class. Please pre-book your spot to l
 et us know you are coming! About the instructor : Tired of disposing of cl
 othes that were still perfectly wearable\, Mike (he/him) started crafting 
 mainly as a means of mending and repair. This led him to knitting (and lat
 er crochet)\, which pretty much immediately became one of his favourite to
 ols of self-expression. Cancellation Policy Classes must be paid for at th
 e time of registration to reserve your spot. - If cancelled 48 hrs or more
  prior to the start of the first class will be given a store credit. Class
 es cancelled less than 48 hrs prior to the start of the class will not be 
 reimbursed.
LOCATION:Bistitchual\, 266 Jane St\, Toronto\, ON M6S 3Z2
URL:https://bistitchual.ca/products/beginner-knitting-course-november-1
X-SOURCE:Bistitchual
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Beginner Crochet - November
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20261122T143000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20261122T160000
UID:bistitchual-10402449490178@bistitchual.ca
DESCRIPTION:This listing is for a two session Beginner Crochet Course. The
  classes will be held in person at Bistitchual on Sunday November 22nd and
  29th from 2:30pm-4:00pm Learn the fundamentals of crochet in this two par
 t class. We will be covering chaining and single crochet\, as well as doub
 le and half-double crochets. Don’t know what any of that means? Great\, 
 you’re in the right place! We’ll provide all the materials\, including
  a simple pattern that teaches you common terms and instructions you’ll 
 encounter in most crochet projects. We will also discuss how to choose the
  appropriate yarn and hook for a project as well as where you can take you
 r crafting after you master these basic techniques. There’s a lot to lea
 rn\, and we’re excited to accompany your beginning in the wonderful craf
 t of crochet! Materials are included! - 50g ball of worsted weight cotton 
 in your choice of colour - 6mm crochet hook Our class size is capped at 4 
 people\, so everyone can receive the attention they need. Mike will share 
 lots of tips and techniques to get you well on your way. About the instruc
 tor: Tired of disposing of clothes that were still perfectly wearable\, Mi
 ke (he/him) started crafting mainly as a means of mending and repair. This
  led him to knitting (and later crochet)\, which pretty much immediately b
 ecame one of his favourite tools of self-expression. Please note that clas
 ses will only proceed if we have a minimum of two attendees . If the minim
 um is not met\, there will be the option for a refund or to reschedule. Th
 ere will be a four person maximum for each class. Please pre-book your spo
 t to let us know you are coming! Cancellation Policy Classes must be paid 
 for at the time of registration to reserve your spot. - If cancelled 48 hr
 s or more prior to the start of the first class will be given a store cred
 it. Classes cancelled less than 48 hrs prior to the start of the class wil
 l not be reimbursed.
LOCATION:Bistitchual\, 266 Jane St\, Toronto\, ON M6S 3Z2
URL:https://bistitchual.ca/products/beginner-crochet-november-1
X-SOURCE:Bistitchual
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Granny Squares 101 - October
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20261017T143000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20261017T163000
UID:bistitchual-10338292695298@bistitchual.ca
DESCRIPTION:This listing is for a Beginner Granny Square Course. The class
 es will be held in person at Bistitchual on Saturday October 17th from 2:3
 0pm - 4:30pm Bring your yarn over and pull through to our two hour granny 
 square class! From blankets\; to sweaters\; to bags\; and much more\, thes
 e cozy squares can be used in a wide range of designs. They’re a joy to 
 make\, simple to reproduce and easy to customize to your own style and pro
 ject needs. This class teaches how to make a basic granny square\, how to 
 change colours and\, how to join squares together. We’ll discuss variati
 ons in construction and further possibilities. We expect students in this 
 class to already know how to chain\, make single and double crochets. You
 ’ll need a 5.0 mm hook and worsted weight yarn in 2-3 colours. Materials
  are not provided\, please bring your own or purchase these supplies at Bi
 stitchual with a 10% discount\, before class begins! Required materials: -
  worsted weight wool in a few different colours - 5.0mm hook About the ins
 tructor: If idle hands are the Devil’s tools\, he hasn’t much to do wi
 th Anna (she/they.) Anna’s grandmother taught her to knit as a toddler a
 nd she hasn’t put the yarn down since. Knitting\, crochet\, spinning\, d
 yeing\, embroidery\, hand sewing\, machine sewing - Anna has a voracious a
 ppetite for learning new textile techniques. With a background in textile 
 artifact conservation\, Anna explores the craft\, history\, and science be
 hind fibre arts. Cancellation Policy Classes must be paid for at the time 
 of registration to reserve your spot. - If cancelled 48 hrs or more prior 
 to the start of the class\, the order will be refunded. Classes cancelled 
 less than 48 hrs prior to the start of the class will not be reimbursed.
LOCATION:Bistitchual\, 266 Jane St\, Toronto\, ON M6S 3Z2
URL:https://bistitchual.ca/products/granny-squares-101-october-1
X-SOURCE:Bistitchual
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Cable Class - November
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20261107T143000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20261107T163000
UID:bistitchual-10336682017026@bistitchual.ca
DESCRIPTION:This listing is for a one session Cable Class. The class will 
 be held in person at Bistitchual on Saturday November 7 from 2:30pm-4:30pm
  Have you been fantasizing about the cable sweater of your dreams? Take a 
 step towards making that dream a reality with our Cables Class and learn t
 he secrets of the deceptively simple yet hugely impactful cable knitting t
 echnique. In this class you will learn cable basics which will allow you t
 o tackle any cable project. Students will work through a small pattern tha
 t exemplifies cable techniques. Students should already be comfortable wit
 h the knit and purl stitches\, ribbing\, and pattern reading. Please bring
  worsted weight yarn and appropriate needles. If you need materials\, you 
 can purchase them in store with a 10% class discount. Cable needles will b
 e provided. Please note that classes will only proceed if we have a minimu
 m of two attendees . If the minimum is not met\, there will be the option 
 for a refund or to reschedule. There will be a four person maximum for eac
 h class. Please pre-book your spot to let us know you are coming! About th
 e Instructor: If idle hands are the Devil’s tools\, he hasn’t much to 
 do with Anna (she/they.) Anna’s grandmother taught her to knit as a todd
 ler and she hasn’t put the yarn down since. Knitting\, crochet\, spinnin
 g\, dyeing\, embroidery\, hand sewing\, machine sewing - Anna has a voraci
 ous appetite for learning new textile techniques. With a background in tex
 tile artifact conservation\, Anna explores the craft\, history\, and scien
 ce behind fibre arts. Cancellation Policy Classes must be paid for at the 
 time of registration to reserve your spot. - If cancelled 48 hrs or more p
 rior to the start of the first class will be given a store credit. Classes
  cancelled less than 48 hrs prior to the start of the class will not be re
 imbursed.
LOCATION:Bistitchual\, 266 Jane St\, Toronto\, ON M6S 3Z2
URL:https://bistitchual.ca/products/cable-class-november
X-SOURCE:Bistitchual
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Learn to Spin Your Own Yarn- November
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20261107T123000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20261107T140000
UID:bistitchual-10336668254466@bistitchual.ca
DESCRIPTION:This listing is for a three session Beginner Spinning Course. 
 The classes will be held in person at Bistitchual on Saturday November 7th
 \, 14\, 21st from 12:30pm - 2:00pm Learn how to transform fibre into yarn 
 with our drop spindle class! In this class you will learn how to use a dro
 p spindle to spin starting with woolly fibre and ending with a completed\,
  ready to use yarn. You will learn how to spin a single ply yarn\, how to 
 spin a 2-ply yarn using the Andean Plying method\, and how to chain ply fo
 r a 3-ply yarn over three classes. We will discuss spinning basics as well
  as different types of yarn\, fibres\, processing tools\, and preparations
  and how these affect the finished yarn. Drop spindles must be brought by 
 students or purchased in store. 50g of fibre provided in two different col
 ours. About the instructor: If idle hands are the Devil’s tools\, he has
 n’t much to do with Anna (she/they.) Anna’s grandmother taught her to 
 knit as a toddler and she hasn’t put the yarn down since. Knitting\, cro
 chet\, spinning\, dyeing\, embroidery\, hand sewing\, machine sewing - Ann
 a has a voracious appetite for learning new textile techniques. With a bac
 kground in textile artifact conservation\, Anna explores the craft\, histo
 ry\, and science behind fibre arts. Please note that classes will only pro
 ceed if we have a minimum of two attendees . If the minimum is not met\, t
 here will be the option for a refund or to reschedule. There will be a fou
 r person maximum for each class. Please pre-book your spot to let us know 
 you are coming! Cancellation Policy Classes must be paid for at the time o
 f registration to reserve your spot. - If cancelled 48 hrs or more prior t
 o the start of the first class will be given a store credit. Classes cance
 lled less than 48 hrs prior to the start of the class will not be reimburs
 ed.
LOCATION:Bistitchual\, 266 Jane St\, Toronto\, ON M6S 3Z2
URL:https://bistitchual.ca/products/learn-to-spin-your-own-yarn-november
X-SOURCE:Bistitchual
END:VEVENT
